  "answer": "To reduce the risk of failing to distinguish genuine AI safety advances from unproductive research, it has been proposed that organizations empirically measure and objectively evaluate both safety and capabilities metrics together (https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.12001, https://www.alignmentforum.org/posts/wpsGprQCRffRKG92v/catastrophic-risks-from-ai-4-organizational-risks). The mechanism for this involves contrasting these two measurements to ensure that safety interventions actually improve safety *relative* to general capabilities, thereby replacing current reliance on intuition, gut feelings, and appeals to authority (https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.12001, https://www.alignmentforum.org/posts/wpsGprQCRffRKG92v/catastrophic-risks-from-ai-4-organizational-risks). By doing so, organizations can demonstrate actual risk reduction and avoid \"safetywashing,\" a phenomenon where general capability advancements are mischaracterized as safety improvements (https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.12001, https://www.alignmentforum.org/posts/wpsGprQCRffRKG92v/catastrophic-risks-from-ai-4-organizational-risks)."
}
